  "published": "2026-09-01T14:57:35.53Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.7.2: FR0139 swaps Seq functions to the Array module where the typed tree proves an array — measured on .NET 10, arrays only, with `contains` on int arrays defaulting to vectorised Enumerable.Contains and offering Array.contains beside it. Rule fixes found by dogfooding and by re-sweeping the corpus: FR0030 no longer emits code that cannot parse for a range source, FR0119 binds only on a computation expression's own statement spine (21 rollbacks in one repo), FR0029 tail extraction stops at a `use` and FR0005 cures the shape an older version wrote, FR0039 keeps backticked receivers, and a failed verification no longer leaves kept fixes suppressed. The benchmarks now target .NET 10. 0.7.1: the published package now reliably carries BOTH analyzer SDK builds flat in analyzers/dotnet/fs — FSharp.Refactor.Analyzers.Ionide.dll for stock Ionide (SDK 0.35.0) and the 0.37.2 build for the CLI and newer FsAutoComplete — plus the review-hardening fixes 0.7.0's rolling pack accumulated; the repository gains a classic Visual Studio extension (VSIX): squiggles and light-bulb fixes in VS 2022-2026 rendered from an FsAutoComplete sidecar. 0.7.0: cross-file migrations arrive — under --api-changes, strictly internal declarations now migrate project-wide with every use classified against its own file (FR0069 voption, FR0093 struct tuples, FR0049 taskify), gated hard: public never, InternalsVisibleTo assemblies never, one unconvertible use vetoes everything. FR0029 grows branch-return tail extraction and per-arm match/match! splitting into nested tasks, and match! arm interiors are finally visible to every rule (an SDK walker hole). Solution runs order narrowest target first and shared directive-free files sweep once across all frameworks and projects; fully-swept compilations skip their typecheck. New rules: FR0132 trailing comments promote to XML docs; FR0133 five-word test names become double-backtick sentences (locals opt-in); FR0134 UtcNow-fed DateTime fields migrate to DateTimeOffset (opt-in); FR0135 markdown-bearing script comments become literate (** cells. FR0022 also mines field names from XAndY case names and clear trailing comments. Everything adversarially audited: keyword field names, fake-clock shadowing, cross-type comparisons, multi-line plain strings under re-indentation, TestCaseSource string references and more are all vetoed by construction. FR0136 states zero-argument Guid constructors as Guid.Empty (the editor also offers NewGuid()); FR0137 fuses consecutive same-module map passes via composition; FR0035 gains the module-level-set quick-fix (in-place Set.ofList when probes are the only uses, a HashSet companion otherwise); FR0039 extends its fix to the method-call shape (path.ToLower().StartsWith \"file:\" becomes the StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase overload, per the .NET string best-practices guide); FR0005 collapses no-op return! task wrappers and unjustified tail thunks; the multi-pass loop warns on non-convergence and blocks a rule that keeps growing the same file, and a failed verification now rolls back only the fixes at the error sites instead of every fix in the file. FR0138 rewrites hand-rolled emptiness tests (isNull x || x = \"\") to String.IsNullOrEmpty/IsNullOrWhiteSpace; FR0139 swaps Seq functions to the Array module where the typed tree proves an array (measured 2.3x on exists, enumerator allocation gone) - arrays only, and never the numeric aggregates that FR0041 sends to vectorised LINQ. 138 rules. 0.6.8: fixes first — a run now prints its fixes and holds advisory notes to one summary line (--notes lists them, --report exports SARIF). FR0029 applies its own FS3511 advice: hoisting pre-await lets (documenting comments travel along), splitting branching tasks per arm, wrapping non-awaiting tails, extracting awaiting try/finally suffixes; the multi-pass loop chains the moves. FR0049 rewrites blocking binds (GetAwaiter().GetResult(), .Result, Async.RunSynchronously) to let!/do! in task and async alike; sync-direction swaps stay config-opt-in. Suppression policy (suppressions: all/no-correctness/none plus --honor-suppressions) and per-rule config parameters. New rules FR0117-FR0131: or-pattern arm folding; CancellationToken omission and None-propagation; awaitable-twin calls; catch blocks logging without the exception (PII-aware); DateTime.Now/UtcNow.Date pitfalls; invalid regexes; Monitor.Enter/Exit to lock; interpolated logging to message templates; invisible/bidi Unicode with escape fixes; process-execution sinks; provider-format API-key literals; obsolete crypto constructors to static factories; guard-equality clauses to literal patterns; module constants gain [<Literal>]; provably tail-recursive functions gain [<TailCall>]. match/match!/function parity for arm rules; SHA1 editor alternatives on FR0065. 130 rules.",
